WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:05.170
How is Marvel’s “Black Panther” franchise
going to continue without Chadwick Boseman?

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:08.680
And what’s with that strange ceremony with
everyone wearing white?

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:12.730
Keep watching to find out more small details
you may have missed in the “Black Panther:

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:15.219
Wakanda Forever” trailer.

00:00:15.219 --> 00:00:17.349
“Wakanda Forever!”

00:00:17.349 --> 00:00:21.259
It's a remarkable achievement that "Black
Panther: Wakanda Forever" even made it to

00:00:21.259 --> 00:00:22.269
the finish line.

00:00:22.269 --> 00:00:26.679
Chadwick Boseman, who plays T'Challa, aka
Black Panther, in the first film, passed away

00:00:26.679 --> 00:00:31.880
at the age of 43 in 2020, leaving behind shoes
that were impossible to fill.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:42.690
"There aren't words to express what an amazing
human being Chadwick Boseman was"

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:46.830
Marvel fans everywhere were captivated by
his performance in "Black Panther," and it's

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:52.640
one of the many factors that led to the film
being nominated for several Academy Awards in 2019.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:57.430
Fortunately, Marvel opted not to try and recast
another actor as T'Challa.

00:00:57.430 --> 00:01:01.820
Instead, it appears the studio will center
the sequel story around T'Challa's younger

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:07.100
sister, Shuri, his mother, Queen Ramonda,
Nakia, Okoye, and other characters from the

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:12.340
2018 movie, all the while finding a way to
honor the legacies of Boseman and his character.

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:16.649
At least, that's what it looks like based
on the first trailer for "Black Panther: Wakanda

00:01:16.649 --> 00:01:20.830
Forever" that debuted on Saturday evening
at San Diego Comic-Con 2022.

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:25.180
The teaser trailer for the second "Black Panther"
feature indicates there is still plenty of

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:27.479
life left in this beloved franchise.

00:01:27.479 --> 00:01:31.869
In addition to boasting plenty of important
characters from the previous movie, the teaser

00:01:31.869 --> 00:01:37.740
introduces the audience to some new players
and hints at other mystical worlds away from Wakanda.

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:41.770
There's plenty to unpack, so let's take a
look at some of the smaller details you may

00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:42.770
have missed.

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:46.740
The first third of the "Black Panther: Wakanda
Forever" trailer shows Wakanda in a state

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:50.960
of mourning for their late king — and most
recent Black Panther — T'Challa.

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:55.329
In the wake of Boseman's death, Ryan Coogler,
director of both "Black Panther" installments,

00:01:55.329 --> 00:02:01.069
addressed the packed SDCC 2022 convention
hall and told fans that Boseman's legacy will

00:02:01.069 --> 00:02:04.590
last far beyond the tragic early end of his
life.

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:10.630
He said, "I promise you, I feel his hand on
me right now, Chad's passion and the genius

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:15.150
and his culture and the impact he made on
this industry will be felt forever."

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:18.660
T'Challa's absence hangs heavy over the beginning
of the trailer.

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:24.960
We get brief glimpses of Shuri, Nakia, Okoye,
and his mother, Queen Ramonda in various displays

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:31.420
of sadness or stoicism while soul sensation
Tems delivers a mournful cover of Bob Marley's

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:33.430
"No Woman, No Cry".

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:38.720
It is very clear that T'Challa's absence cuts
deep in the lives of everyone who knew him,

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:43.580
loved him, and fought beside him, leaving
them all to shed a tear privately or come

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:44.880
together as one.

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:48.750
“And my entire family is gone!”

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:53.900
We also see a large ceremony featuring a cadre
of dancers and a ceremonial procession, but

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:55.470
everyone wears white.

00:02:55.470 --> 00:03:01.000
As such, it's unclear if this is a funeral
procession for T'Challa, a wedding (for Shuri,

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:03.290
perhaps?), or something else entirely.

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:08.230
As you would expect from the most senior surviving
member of the Wakandan royal family, Ramonda

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:13.400
is leading by example as the stone-cold and
determined figurehead of the nation.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:17.550
After being separated from both her children
during The Blip in "Avengers: Infinity War,"

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:21.670
and then happily reunited with them at the
end of "Avengers: Endgame," the stress has

00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:27.040
clearly taken a toll on her based on the wisps
of white hair poking out from under her headdress

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.230
as she gazes across the beach.

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:34.760
Ramonda appears to be navigating the very
public, very exacting duty of leading a nation

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:37.420
while struggling with the death of her son.

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:42.500
It's a tough road ahead for the queen, but
she has the support she needs to get her through.

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:47.080
This includes her daughter Shuri, who is by
her side and ready to put on a strong front.

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:51.150
But it doesn't seem like the Wakandan princess
will focus much on her brilliant engineering

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:55.090
skills — or, at least, they’ll take a
backseat to more important matters.

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:59.069
At one point in the "Black Panther: Wakanda
Forever" teaser trailer, we see her participating

00:03:59.069 --> 00:04:03.060
in the royal duties, including taking part
in what appears to be a funeral procession

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:05.760
(unless it's something more celebratory?)

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:07.750
and recruiting help from Riri Williams.

00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:13.000
Yes, that's right — fans will meet Ironheart
before she takes the spotlight in her upcoming

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:15.430
solo Disney+ series of the same name.

00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:20.450
Of all the exciting details that the new teaser
for "Black Panther: Wakanda Forever" offers,

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:24.910
seeing Namor and the rest of the Atlanteans
for the first time will probably make Marvel

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:27.260
fans jump right out of their seats.

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:31.690
Not even one minute into the trailer, fans
can see what appears to be an Atlantean couple

00:04:31.690 --> 00:04:36.100
giving birth to a new child — which could
possibly be a young Namor.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:40.660
In a haunting shot just past the one-minute
mark, it appears that Atlanteans and what

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:43.840
might be a young Namor are watching a building
burn.

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:48.370
It then immediately transitions to him walking
out of the water as an adult, appearing far

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:52.380
more stately and adorned with additional Atlantean
regalia.

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:55.570
We also get plenty of shots of the Atlantean
community.

00:04:55.570 --> 00:05:00.820
The trailer isn't shy with its breathtaking
shots of the underwater way of life the citizens

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:02.460
of Atlantis live.

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:07.120
Scenes of a crew of Atlanteans riding a humpback
whale and a squad of Atlantean fighters facing

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:12.220
off against an unseen foe on dry land are
sure to stick in our minds until we see this movie.

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:17.240
Marvel Comics' Atlanteans have been around
on Earth for some time, along with Namor,

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:20.820
although they technically immigrated from
the planet Vodan long ago.

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:24.990
Namor is the son of a human father and an
Atlantean princess.

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:29.760
He is also one of the most powerful and intelligent
beings in the Marvel universe.

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:33.400
In fact, in Marvel Comics, Namor has been
part of the Illuminati, the group that makes

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:37.960
their live-action debut in "Doctor Strange
in the Multiverse of Madness."

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:44.419
"Wanda stop, you possessed an innocent woman
but you can still do the right thing: let her go."

00:05:44.419 --> 00:05:48.690
It will be interesting to see what we learn
of Namor and the origins of the Atlanteans

00:05:48.690 --> 00:05:53.060
in the MCU — as they are known to make alterations
from comic’s origins sometimes.

00:05:53.060 --> 00:05:58.350
IGN first reported in August 2021 that Riri
Williams — also known as Ironheart – would

00:05:58.350 --> 00:06:02.190
appear in "Black Panther: Wakanda Forever,"
and the new trailer confirms it.

00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:06.510
Played by Dominique Thorne, Riri Williams
is a relatively newer character in Marvel

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:07.510
comics history.

00:06:07.510 --> 00:06:12.620
A genius, Riri is only a teenager when she
begins her studies at the Massachusetts Institute

00:06:12.620 --> 00:06:18.210
of Technology, where she creates an advanced
suit of armor in honor of her favorite hero, Iron Man.

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:22.560
In the "Black Panther: Wakanda Forever" trailer,
Riri is first greeted in Shuri's lab with

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:25.900
a hand slap from the Wakandan royal, who seems
to know her well.

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:30.800
Later, Queen Ramonda delivers a speech and
asks, "Have I not given everything?"

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:33.010
as various scenes play in the background.

00:06:33.010 --> 00:06:37.320
One of those scenes seems to show Riri forging
her Ironheart suit of armor as a piece of

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:39.400
heart-shaped armor falls to the floor.

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:44.080
It looks like we'll not only get to meet Riri,
but we'll also get to see her in action as

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:46.030
the metal-clad superhero.

00:06:46.030 --> 00:06:50.350
It's unclear how large of a role Ironheart
will play in the forthcoming "Black Panther"

00:06:50.350 --> 00:06:53.720
sequel, but the character's future looks bright
in the MCU.

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:58.850
Aside from the riveting performance by Chadwick
Boseman in the titular role, one of the biggest

00:06:58.850 --> 00:07:02.360
standouts in "Black Panther" was his nemesis,
Killmonger.

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:07.110
Micheal B. Jordan's take on the villain brought
a solid performance of a grounded and somewhat

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:10.080
relatable opposition to T'Challa's claim to
the throne.

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:15.310
The fact that one could watch "Black Panther"
and not wholly disagree with his perspective

00:07:15.310 --> 00:07:19.370
made Killmonger one of the best villains in
the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:23.390
While fans on Reddit have wondered if they
would see Jordan return as T'Challa's villainous

00:07:23.390 --> 00:07:27.750
cousin, his death at the end of the 2018 hit
pic made it unlikely.

00:07:27.750 --> 00:07:32.330
The trailer, however, gives us a sneak peek
at the new Black Panther suit at the end.

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:37.040
Opening its claws on a beach and preparing
for battle, it is almost impossible not to

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:39.710
notice the signature gold details.

00:07:39.710 --> 00:07:42.190
Those elements are not on the suit worn by
T'Challa.

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:48.725
Instead, they adorn the suit worn by Killmonger
in the cousins' climactic "Black Panther" face-off.

00:07:48.725 --> 00:07:51.310
His suit seems to be back, but is Killmonger
returning as well?

